Subject: [PATCH] GB10 downloads, failed captures, Engram ids, opt-in draft calibration on 2 x DGX Spark (both ranks)

On top of 0064 (the bundle-14 tree), bundle 16, carrying fixes others found for this hardware and engine family.
On an integrated GPU (GB10 reports CU_DEVICE_ATTRIBUTE_INTEGRATED = 1) every synchronous device-to-host copy lands in a
per-thread 4 MiB pinned bounce first, because with driver 580.178.04 a cuMemcpyDtoH straight into pageable memory can
return success with pages left as they were (TensorFold upstream, ashhart/TensorFold a3962b45, 194115d2, e9ee7383,
Apache-2.0); the drafter's two reads every pass go this way. A stretch that fails inside its CUDA graph capture joins
what it forked, ends the capture and clears its flags, so the next capture does not wait on the dead one's event and
fail with 901 until a restart (ldenaeyer, MiaAI-Lab/DeepSeek-v4.1-Flash-1017-2x-DGX-Sparks pull request #119,
Apache-2.0); a round that fails also waits out the Engram reads it submitted. Engram row ids are checked before a read
batch allocates (Blackwellboy, bertholomus/TensorFold 12132870, Apache-2.0). MiaAI-Lab's 0050 per-stream draft-survival
calibration (Apache-2.0) is ported, off unless TF_DS_T25_DRAFT_CAL is set, with one change: a calibrated head granted
no drafts moves back toward no correction, so it is measured again. Tokens are unchanged with the calibration unset.
CPU-tested with twelve red copies (757 test executions), source-reviewed twice, and A/B-checked on the pair: 92/92 exact
against 0064 (research/LOCAL-STACK-20261106.md, "Bundle 16"). Generated with `git diff --binary` in a checkout of the
0064 tree; `git apply` of it gives the served source file for file (1287 files, sha256-compared).

